1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,694
A 3D model on a page is only half the job.

2
00:00:02,754 --> 00:00:07,224
How it's lit, how far away the camera
sits, what a customer is allowed to do

3
00:00:07,284 --> 00:00:08,952
with it — that's all in here.

4
00:00:10,162 --> 00:00:13,610
The viewer settings card sits under the
model file, on the left.

5
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:18,050
Everything you change here is saved to
that product's own config metafield, so it

6
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:21,887
applies to this product only and overrides
the theme block's defaults.

7
00:00:22,747 --> 00:00:26,263
On the right is the live preview, and this
is the thing to trust.

8
00:00:26,323 --> 00:00:30,829
It renders the same viewer your customers
get, loading the same file the storefront

9
00:00:30,889 --> 00:00:31,489
will.

10
00:00:31,164 --> 00:00:34,791
Nothing here needs saving to see — the
preview updates as you drag.

11
00:00:35,651 --> 00:00:36,703
Start with Display.

12
00:00:36,763 --> 00:00:41,619
Viewer height sets how tall the viewer is
on the page, from two hundred up to twelve

13
00:00:41,679 --> 00:00:42,496
hundred pixels.

14
00:00:42,556 --> 00:00:44,545
Drag it and watch the preview grow.

15
00:00:45,405 --> 00:00:48,563
Background colour is the one setting
people change first.

16
00:00:48,623 --> 00:00:53,023
Pick a colour that matches your theme — a
white viewer dropped into a dark page

17
00:00:53,083 --> 00:00:54,265
reads as a broken box.

18
00:00:54,325 --> 00:00:56,692
You can use the swatch or type a hex
value.

19
00:00:57,552 --> 00:01:01,915
Exposure is brightness, and it's the fix
for a model that came out of Blender

20
00:01:01,975 --> 00:01:03,638
looking too dark or blown out.

21
00:01:03,698 --> 00:01:06,625
Zero to five, and small moves make a big
difference.

22
00:01:07,485 --> 00:01:12,311
Tone mapping decides how bright values get
compressed into what your screen can show.

23
00:01:12,371 --> 00:01:13,863
Linear is the safe default.

24
00:01:13,923 --> 00:01:18,692
ACES Filmic is the most photographic and
usually the best-looking for product

25
00:01:18,752 --> 00:01:20,359
Try them — it's one dropdown.

26
00:01:21,219 --> 00:01:22,910
Three switches finish Display.

27
00:01:22,970 --> 00:01:27,405
Default environment map generates lighting
so metals and glossy plastics have

28
00:01:27,465 --> 00:01:29,449
something to reflect — leave it on.

29
00:01:29,509 --> 00:01:31,842
Blur skybox softens the background image.

30
00:01:31,902 --> 00:01:36,337
And Cast shadow puts a contact shadow
under the model, which is what stops it

31
00:01:36,397 --> 00:01:37,913
looking like it's floating.

32
00:01:38,773 --> 00:01:42,178
Environment is for when the generated
lighting isn't enough.

33
00:01:42,238 --> 00:01:46,451
Point Skybox at an HDR image and it
becomes the visible background and the

34
00:01:46,511 --> 00:01:47,202
light source.

35
00:01:47,262 --> 00:01:51,591
Environment map is a separate HDR used
only for reflections, so you can have

36
00:01:51,651 --> 00:01:54,767
studio lighting on the model without a
photo behind it.

37
00:01:55,627 --> 00:01:56,227
Camera.

38
00:01:56,031 --> 00:02:00,819
FOV mode is Auto by default, which frames
the model to fit whatever its size happens

39
00:02:00,879 --> 00:02:03,590
to be — leave it there unless you have a
reason.

40
00:02:03,650 --> 00:02:08,149
Switch to Custom and the FOV slider wakes
up: low numbers are a long lens, high

41
00:02:08,209 --> 00:02:09,650
numbers a wide-angle look.

42
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:14,516
Initial yaw and pitch are the angle the
model faces when the page loads.

43
00:02:14,576 --> 00:02:19,090
This is worth spending a minute on: turn
the shoe so the logo faces the customer,

44
00:02:19,150 --> 00:02:20,954
tilt it so they can see the sole.

45
00:02:21,014 --> 00:02:23,043
Watch the preview rotate as you drag.

46
00:02:23,903 --> 00:02:27,001
Initial zoom moves the camera in or out
from that framing.

47
00:02:27,061 --> 00:02:28,580
Positive numbers move closer.

48
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:32,936
Combined with yaw and pitch, these three
give you a proper hero shot rather than

49
00:02:32,996 --> 00:02:35,114
whatever angle the file was exported at.

50
00:02:35,974 --> 00:02:38,423
Controls decide what a customer can do.

51
00:02:38,483 --> 00:02:41,898
Allow rotate, allow pan, allow zoom — all
independent.

52
00:02:41,958 --> 00:02:47,239
Turning pan on is useful for large models;
turning zoom off is useful when you want

53
00:02:47,299 --> 00:02:48,719
one fixed presentation.

54
00:02:49,579 --> 00:02:51,872
Auto rotate spins the model gently on
load.

55
00:02:51,932 --> 00:02:56,249
It's the single best way to tell a shopper
that this image is interactive — most

56
00:02:56,309 --> 00:02:59,750
people won't try to drag a picture unless
something moves first.

57
00:03:00,610 --> 00:03:02,008
These two matter on mobile.

58
00:03:02,068 --> 00:03:06,382
Page scroll on touch lets a finger drag
scroll the page instead of trapping it in

59
00:03:06,442 --> 00:03:07,678
the viewer — keep it on.

60
00:03:07,738 --> 00:03:11,998
Page scroll on mouse wheel does the same
for the wheel, so the wheel scrolls the

61
00:03:12,058 --> 00:03:13,888
page rather than zooming the model.

62
00:03:14,748 --> 00:03:18,818
Control bar is the on-screen buttons, each
one an individual switch.

63
00:03:18,878 --> 00:03:23,860
By default you get zoom in, zoom out, and
fullscreen — that's a deliberate minimum,

64
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:26,228
so the model isn't buried under chrome.

65
00:03:27,088 --> 00:03:30,534
Switch the rest on and you can see them
appear in the preview.

66
00:03:30,594 --> 00:03:32,400
The axis gizmo shows orientation.

67
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:35,453
The camera button downloads a PNG of the
current view.

68
00:03:35,513 --> 00:03:38,167
Reset returns the camera to your starting
angle.

69
00:03:38,227 --> 00:03:42,464
And the animation switcher shows the
playing clip — note that with this off,

70
00:03:42,524 --> 00:03:44,330
the model doesn't animate at all.

71
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:45,790
Animation.

72
00:03:45,831 --> 00:03:51,088
If your model has clips baked in, default
animation index picks which one autoplays

73
00:03:51,148 --> 00:03:52,369
— zero is the first.

74
00:03:52,429 --> 00:03:57,366
Repeat mode: one loops that clip, all
cycles through every clip, none plays it

75
00:03:57,426 --> 00:03:58,327
once and stops.

76
00:03:59,187 --> 00:04:02,207
AR lets a shopper put the product in their
room.

77
00:04:02,267 --> 00:04:06,442
WebXR and Google Scene Viewer cover
Android and are on by default.

78
00:04:06,502 --> 00:04:11,575
Apple Quick Look covers iPhone and iPad,
but it needs a separate USDZ file — glb

79
00:04:11,635 --> 00:04:16,516
won't do — so upload one to Shopify Files
and paste its URL in the box below.

80
00:04:17,376 --> 00:04:19,563
Advanced holds two specialist options.

81
00:04:19,623 --> 00:04:24,294
Material variant switches the model to a
named variant, if your glb was authored

82
00:04:24,354 --> 00:04:26,245
with them — handy for colourways.

83
00:04:26,305 --> 00:04:30,976
And fix skinned bounding box recalculates
the model's bounds using its skeleton,

84
00:04:31,036 --> 00:04:34,170
which fixes rigged models that frame
themselves badly.

85
00:04:35,030 --> 00:04:37,517
Nothing is stored until you hit Save
settings.

86
00:04:37,577 --> 00:04:41,448
The button only lights up when you
actually have unsaved changes, so it

87
00:04:41,508 --> 00:04:43,220
doubles as your dirty indicator.

88
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:48,548
Once saved, a Customized chip appears next
to the product name, and a Reset to

89
00:04:48,608 --> 00:04:50,755
defaults button appears in the header.

90
00:04:50,815 --> 00:04:55,225
Reset deletes the config metafield
entirely, so the product falls back to the

91
00:04:55,285 --> 00:04:56,560
theme block's defaults.

92
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:58,483
That's every setting.

93
00:04:58,543 --> 00:05:02,813
Next, the three different ways this app
lets you check your work before customers

94
00:05:02,873 --> 00:05:03,473
see it.
